  "title": "Merge Sort Algorithm",
  "story": "How does a large list get sorted efficiently? Imagine splitting a shuffled deck of cards in half repeatedly until every pile has just one card. Then, merge pairs of piles back together in sorted order by comparing their top cards until you have one single sorted deck. This divide-and-conquer strategy is merge sort. We can trace its steps to see how breaking a problem down makes it simple to solve.",
  "cardDescription": "Explore how merge sort divides a collection into single elements and merges them back in order. Follow each step to see the divide-and-conquer strategy in action.",
